===Etymology===
{{etymon|en|:inh|enm:persoun|tree=1}}
From {{inh|en|enm|persoun}}, {{m|enm|personne}} et al., from {{der|en|xno|parsone}}, {{m|fro|persoun}} et al. ({{cog|fro|persone}}, {{cog|fr|personne}}), and its source {{der|en|la|persōna|t=mask used by actor; role, part, character}}, perhaps a loanword from {{der|en|ett|𐌘𐌄𐌓𐌔𐌖|t=mask}}. In this sense, displaced native {{m|en|man}}, which came to mean primarily "adult male" in Middle English; see {{ncog|ang|mann}}. Displaced native {{noncog|ang|hād||person, individual}}. {{doublet|en|parson|persona}}.

